# LeakSanitizer suppressions for bugs that are known, understood and NOT reachable on Ruby.
# fuzz/run.sh passes this file in LSAN_OPTIONS. Every entry says why it is safe and when
# to remove it. Never add an entry for a bug in Ruby's own code: fix it instead.

# libwally 1.5.6 (our submodule, 3bf543cd): wally_psbt_from_bytes() with
# WALLY_PSBT_PARSE_FLAG_LOOSE leaks the input/output arrays of a PSBT that carries
# PSBT_GLOBAL_UNSIGNED_TX before PSBT_GLOBAL_VERSION = 2 (psbt_set_global_tx() allocates
# them, the v2 path overwrites the pointers). Found by fuzz_psbt_from_bytes on 2026-11-18
# with the vector "PSBTv0 but with PSBT_GLOBAL_VERSION set to 2" of libwally's psbt.json.
# Not reachable on Ruby: Ruby parses every PSBT with STRICT | COMPLETE
# (main/process/sign_psbt.c, deserialise_psbt()), which refuses that PSBT first.
# Fixed upstream in libwally 10f41d80 (2026-11-08, release_1.6.1).
# REMOVE when components/libwally-core/upstream is at release_1.6.1 or later.
leak:psbt_set_global_tx
